    "description": "The Terrova QUEST is the bow mount to buy if you want the motor to do the boat handling for you. Retailers list it at 90 lb of thrust on 24V and 115 lb on 36V, in 45-, 60- and 72-inch shafts, with a bolt-on bow mount and a maximum amp draw of 58 A. Its headline feature is Spot-Lock, Minn Kota's GPS anchoring, which listings say you can trigger from the wireless remote or a compatible Humminbird fish finder; the included heading sensor adds Jog, which moves your locked position five feet in any direction, and AutoPilot holds a heading. The standard versions have Dual Spectrum CHIRP sonar built into the motor, with the transducer wired through the shaft, and a separate version uses MEGA Side and Down Imaging. Retailer prices run from about $3,400 to $3,800 depending on shaft length, and several listings showed it out of stock, so check availability. Listings give a two-year warranty. This is a freshwater motor and needs a 24V or 36V battery bank, which is a real added cost.",
    "pros": [
