          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best trolling motor is the one sized to your loaded boat and your water. For most small freshwater boats, the <strong class="text-white">Minn Kota Endura C2 55</strong> is the dependable default. For bass and pontoon boats where holding position matters, a GPS bow mount like the <strong class="text-white">Minn Kota Terrova QUEST</strong> or, on a 12V saltwater boat, the <strong class="text-white">MotorGuide Xi5 with Pinpoint GPS</strong> is the upgrade worth paying for.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you choose, get the thrust, shaft length and battery right before you compare brands, check the exact product code for shaft length, buy a saltwater model if you ever fish salt, and register the boat if your state requires it.
